WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.400
Hang onto your wands because Harry Potter
is back!

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.400
Well … sort of.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.940
Our favorite Boy Wizard isn't gracing the
big screen again, but his Wizarding World

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.309
has expanded, shedding some light on one of
the series' previously little-known characters:

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:13.730
Newt Scamander.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.970
Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them introduces
a fuller version of the guy previously best

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.960
known in the Potter universe for writing a
wizarding textbook.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.791
And while the new series starter introduces
a distinct time, setting, characters, and

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:28.780
even vocabulary elements, there were some
subtle nods to the Harry Potter faithful you

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:29.910
might've missed.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.730
And of course, let's not forget the magic
words: spoilers ahead.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.000
Making a name

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.590
The biggest tie-in between Scamander and the
Potter universe — well, apart from being

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.500
a wizard, of course — is the fact that he
once wrote the book on magizoology that would

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.710
later be taught at Hogwarts.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.760
Fantastic Beasts takes place long before Newt's
anthology would become a part of Hogwarts'

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.310
curriculum, so it was something of a nod to
the Potter realm that Newt's new gal Tina

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.910
gives its manuscript the name we all know.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.239
That tiny-giant suitcase

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:01.430
The fact that Newt's suitcase had a limitless
interior size was certainly a callback to

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.700
things we'd seen in the Harry Potter series
before.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.319
Consider how massive the Weasleys' Quidditch
World Cup tent was on the inside.

00:01:07.319 --> 00:01:11.780
The visual element of the attache being opened
by prying claws too, seemed like a distinct

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:20.600
wink to that sassy The Monster Book of Monsters
that tormented Harry in Prisoner of Azkaban.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.770
Hufflepuff pride

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.950
Even though he's no longer in good standing
within the halls of Hogwarts, Newt Scamander

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:30.429
obviously doesn't hold anything against his
old house, as evidenced by the Hufflepuff-colored

00:01:30.429 --> 00:01:32.340
scarf tucked away in his briefcase.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.160
"The best wizarding school in the world is
Hogwarts."

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.650
"Hogwash."

00:01:38.249 --> 00:01:42.029
It's a good thing he's not bitter towards
his old institution, because we know his future

00:01:42.029 --> 00:01:47.179
grandson, Rolf, is due to marry Hogwarts'
resident weirdo, Luna Lovegood down the line.

00:01:47.179 --> 00:01:48.420
Quidditch quip

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.109
Quidditch was a beloved aspect of the wizarding
world throughout the Harry Potter series,

00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:55.869
and Newt makes a small reference to the sport
when he's asked whether he's a seeker.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:56.880
His response?

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.109
He's "more of a chaser, really."

00:01:58.109 --> 00:02:01.009
That, of course, is a reference to his choice
of field position.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.079
But perhaps if he had spent more time seeking
the Golden Snitch, it would've better prepared

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:08.179
him for the beast-grappling duties in this
installment.

00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:10.039
Merlin's beard!

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:14.129
Even though American muggles are called "no-majs"
and there's plenty of other new terminology

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:18.140
to take in during Fantastic Beasts, there's
one turn of phrase that's a direct quote of

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:21.550
a line from the Harry Potter films: "Merlin's
beard!"

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:25.100
Where've you heard that before?

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.520
"Merlin's beard!"

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:31.019
There are also some familiar spells and wizarding
entryways, and this floating apple that eats

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:34.830
itself in front of the boy is as direct a
wink to Potter as they come.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.400
Behold, the Niffler

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.549
The niffler might be new to the big screen
with Fantastic Beasts, but the adorable mole-duck-porcupine-mix

00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:44.610
creature has long existed in the written realm
of magic.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.380
Although the fantastic beast never made the
cinematic cut for Goblet of Fire, he gets

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.239
more than adequate screen time in Fantastic
Beasts.

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:54.930
There are other creatures who'd been mentioned
before but only made their screen debut in

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:59.840
Fantastic Beasts — including the size-shifting
Occamy and the disappearing Demiguise — but

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.450
the niffler is the real adorable hero of this
movie.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:04.870
Dumbledore before

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:08.489
We didn't get to see our favorite headmaster
in Fantastic Beasts, but he did get a major

00:03:08.489 --> 00:03:11.310
mention that proves he's alive and well as
this movie unfolds.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:15.060
"Thrown out of Hogwarts for endangering human
life."

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.640
"That was an accident."

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.819
"With a beast.

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:22.659
Yet one of your teachers argued strongly against
your expulsion.

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:28.629
Now, what makes Albus Dumbledore so fond of
you?"

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:33.069
We can probably expect to actually see him
show up in the next installments of this series,

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:36.180
because there's another important character
coming into play as well that he'll have a

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.560
lot to do with...

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.140
Gellert Grindelwald 2.0

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.670
Polyjuice Potion impersonations ran rampant
throughout the Harry Potter series, so perhaps

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.640
the big twist in Fantastic Beasts — that
is, that Gellert Grindelwald had disguised

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:52.609
himself as Percival Graves throughout most
of the events of the movie — shouldn't have

00:03:52.609 --> 00:03:53.609
been a surprise.

00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:56.980
But the reintroduction of Grindelwald does
set the stage for some interesting character

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:00.269
history to come, especially when it comes
to Professor Dumbledore.

00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:03.909
In the final Harry Potter movies, we learned
that the pair once worked together to recover

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:07.439
the Deathly Hallows in hopes of making the
world a better place, but their friendship

00:04:07.439 --> 00:04:10.650
soured after Grindelwald began dabbling in
the Dark Arts.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.760
Their duel to come will be one for the ages.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.139
Lestrange family history

00:04:15.139 --> 00:04:19.410
The Lestrange family became a major part of
the mayhem that arose at Lord Voldemort's

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.730
end, but Fantastic Beasts proves there was
more to their backstory than we might've guessed.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:27.320
Before Bellatrix and Narcissa carried the
family into the Dark Lord's corner, there

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.320
was Leta.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.100
Leta LeStrange doesn't get much discussion
in the first Fantastic Beasts movie, but we

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.980
do find out she was a former friend-slash-flame
of Newt's — who apparently betrayed him.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.790
Count on her to come back and have some part
in Gellert Grindelwald's attempt to establish

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.600
a new world order for sure.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.880
The Deathly Hallows

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:47.700
If there's one thing that could not be hidden
during Fantastic Beasts it's the symbolism

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:48.980
of the Deathly Hallows.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:53.720
In the movie, Grindelwald, posing as Graves,
gives our new pal Credence a Deathly Hallows

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.320
necklace, much like the ones we'd seen before
in the Harry Potter movies.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.910
This is also a clear reminder that the Deathly
Hallows are going to be a big part of the

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:01.910
battle to come.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.320
"I wanna be a wizard!"

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.860
Thanks for watching!

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.360
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.590
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

